diff --git a/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md b/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
index a4f48b5..0c2ad81 100644
--- a/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
+++ b/docs/api/sections/webhooks.md
@@ -2,6 +2,14 @@
 
 Webhooks notify another application when something happens on a board. Only account admins can list, view, create, update, delete, or reactivate webhooks.
 
+## Receiving deliveries
+
+When a subscribed event occurs on a board, Fizzy queues one JSON `POST` to each active webhook subscribed to that event. A standard payload contains the event's `id`, `action`, `created_at`, `board` (ID), `creator` (ID and name), `eventable` (type, ID and URL), and action-specific `particulars`. Slack, Campfire, and Basecamp endpoints receive a message formatted for the chat service instead.
+
+Verify `X-Webhook-Signature` by computing the hex-encoded HMAC-SHA256 of the raw request body using the webhook's signing secret. `X-Webhook-Delivery` identifies the delivery, and `X-Webhook-Timestamp` gives the send time in UTC.
+
+Delivery URLs must point to publicly reachable HTTP or HTTPS endpoints. A `2xx` response is a success. Fizzy does not follow redirects or retry failed or uncertain attempts: if the connection drops, the receiver may already have processed the POST. The delivery log shows the result and is retained for one week. A webhook is disabled once it has failed at least ten times in a row and at least an hour has passed since the first failure in that streak. A successful delivery or manual reactivation resets the streak.
+
